{"cid:47965":{"key":"cid:47965","title":"Cefadroxil","compound":{"key":"cid:47965","cid":47965,"qid":"Q2319020","title":"Cefadroxil","iupac":"(6R,7R)-7-[[(2R)-2-amino-2-(4-hydroxyphenyl)acetyl]amino]-3-methyl-8-oxo-5-thia-1-azabicyclo[4.2.0]oct-2-ene-2-carboxylic acid","wiki_url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cefadroxil","cas":"50370-12-2","iuphar":"4831","drugbank":"DB01140","chemspider":"43630","unii":"Q525PA8JJB","kegg":"C06878; D00257","chebi":"3479","chembl":"CHEMBL1644","pdb_ligand":null,"comptox":"DTXSID8022749","echa":"100.051.397","description":"antibiotic","kind":null,"atc":"J01DB05","mesh":null,"uniprot":null,"ncbi_taxon":null,"gbif":null,"powo":null,"extra_at":"2026-11-08T19:46:28+00:00","eml":null,"smiles":"CC1=C(N2[C@@H]([C@@H](C2=O)NC(=O)[C@@H](C3=CC=C(C=C3)O)N)SC1)C(=O)O","chembl_phase":4.0,"first_approval":1978,"bbw":0,"fda":1,"ema":1,"control":null,"reg_at":"2026-11-10T10:42:26+00:00"},"status":null,"pharm":[{"section":"Drug Indication","items":[{"section":"Drug Indication","text":"For the treatment of the following infections (skin, UTI, ENT) caused by; S. pneumoniae, H. influenzae, staphylococci, S. pyogenes (group A beta-hemolytic streptococci), E. coli, P. mirabilis, Klebsiella sp, coagulase-negative staphylococci and Streptococcus pyogenes","source":"DrugBank","url":"https://go.drugbank.com/drugs/DB01140","license_url":"https://www.drugbank.ca/legal/terms_of_use"},{"section":"Drug Indication","text":"FDA Label","source":"DrugBank","url":"https://go.drugbank.com/drugs/DB01140","license_url":"https://www.drugbank.ca/legal/terms_of_use"}]},{"section":"MeSH Pharmacological Classification","items":[{"section":"MeSH Pharmacological Classification","text":"Substances that inhibit the growth or reproduction of BACTERIA.","source":"Medical Subject Headings (MeSH)","url":"https://id.nlm.nih.gov/mesh/M0448397.html","license_url":"https://www.nlm.nih.gov/copyright.html"}]},{"section":"Drug Classes","items":[{"section":"Drug Classes","text":"Breast Feeding; Lactation; Milk, Human; Anti-Infective Agents; Antibacterial Agents; Cephalosporins","source":"Drugs and Lactation Database (LactMed)","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/n/lactmed/LM42/","license_url":"https://www.nlm.nih.gov/copyright.html"}]},{"section":"Pharmacodynamics","items":[{"section":"Pharmacodynamics","text":"Cefadroxil, a first-generation cephalosporin antibiotic, is used to treat urinary tract infections, skin and skin structure infections, pharyngitis, and tonsillitis.","source":"DrugBank","url":"https://go.drugbank.com/drugs/DB01140","license_url":"https://www.drugbank.ca/legal/terms_of_use"}]},{"section":"Mechanism of Action","items":[{"section":"Mechanism of Action","text":"Like all beta-lactam antibiotics, cefadroxil binds to specific penicillin-binding proteins (PBPs) located inside the bacterial cell wall, causing the inhibition of the third and last stage of bacterial cell wall synthesis. Cell lysis is then mediated by bacterial cell wall autolytic enzymes such as autolysins; it is possible that cefadroxil interferes with an autolysin inhibitor.","source":"DrugBank","url":"https://go.drugbank.com/drugs/DB01140","license_url":"https://www.drugbank.ca/legal/terms_of_use"}]},{"section":"Absorption, Distribution and Excretion","items":[{"section":"Absorption, Distribution and Excretion","text":"Cefadroxil is well absorbed on oral administration; food does not interfere with its absorption.","source":"DrugBank","url":"https://go.drugbank.com/drugs/DB01140","license_url":"https://www.drugbank.ca/legal/terms_of_use"},{"section":"Absorption, Distribution and Excretion","text":"Over 90% of the drug is excreted unchanged in the urine within 24 hours. Cefadroxil was detected in the placenta and breast milk.","source":"DrugBank","url":"https://go.drugbank.com/drugs/DB01140","license_url":"https://www.drugbank.ca/legal/terms_of_use"}]},{"section":"Protein Binding","items":[{"section":"Protein Binding","text":"Binding rates of cefadroxil were 28.1% by U.F. method","source":"DrugBank","url":"https://go.drugbank.com/drugs/DB01140","license_url":"https://www.drugbank.ca/legal/terms_of_use"}]},{"section":"Biological Half-Life","items":[{"section":"Biological Half-Life","text":"1.5 hours","source":"DrugBank","url":"https://go.drugbank.com/drugs/DB01140","license_url":"https://www.drugbank.ca/legal/terms_of_use"}]}],"safety":[{"section":"Effects During Pregnancy and Lactation","items":[{"section":"Effects During Pregnancy and Lactation","text":"◉ Summary of Use during Lactation Cefadroxil is no longer marketed in in the US. Limited information indicates that cefadroxil produces low levels in milk that are not expected to cause adverse effects in breastfed infants. Occasionally disruption of the infant's gastrointestinal flora, resulting in diarrhea or thrush have been reported with cephalosporins, but these effects have not been adequately evaluated. Cefadroxil is acceptable in nursing mothers. ◉ Effects in Breastfed Infants Relevant published information was not found as of the revision date. ◉ Effects on Lactation and Breastmilk Relevant published information was not found as of the revision date.","source":"Drugs and Lactation Database (LactMed)","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/n/lactmed/LM42/"}]}],"manufacturing":[],"structure":true,"populations":{"child":{"label":"Suitable for children","count":14,"forms":[["Powder for Oral Suspension",12],["Powder for oral solution",1],["Dispersible Tablet",1]]},"noswallow":{"label":"No tablet or capsule to swallow","count":14,"forms":[["Powder for Oral Suspension",12],["Powder for oral solution",1],["Dispersible Tablet",1]]}},"reg":{"fda":1,"ema":1,"phase":4.0,"first_approval":1978,"bbw":false,"control":null,"withdrawn":[],"reg_checked":true,"aware":{"name":"Cefadroxil","class":"First-generation-cephalosporins","atc":"J01DB05","category":"Access","eml":false}},"chem":{"props":{"key":"cid:47965","title":"Cefadroxil","products":22,"mw":363.4,"logp":0.15,"tpsa":133.0,"